<http://data.silknow.org/object/cdc49da1-b1e2-323b-b0af-42fc1c391127/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Typographical silk programme printed in salmon-pink lettering on a cream programme with an integral fringe top and bottom, headed with the name of the theatre 'THE NEW Empire Variety Theatre NEWGATE STREET, NEWCASTLE' in upper and lower case lettering, followed by the names of the Lessees, Messrs. Moss & Thornton; the General Manager Mr. J.G. Allen; the Acting Manager Mr. J. Pellow, and the Musical Director Mr. J.W. Dawson. 'GRAND AFTERNOON PERFORMANCE FOR THE BENEFIT of the NEWCASTLE INFIMARY' is printed below the list of the management, with the date WEDNESDAY 28th OCTOBER 1891. This is followed by a list of the seventeen acts, and in much smaller typeface the name and address of the printer."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/cdc49da1-b1e2-323b-b0af-42fc1c391127> .

